（複選）Consider a general recursive mechanism <b>R</b>, whose input is an array A() initially with n elements. The pseudo code of R is listed below, It takes a parameter k, use √n (n is the size of A when applied, n may change) steps to partition <b>A</b>, and may call another function Q, whose complexity may vary and depends on the size of its input.<pre>Procedure R (array A with size n, int k)
1. if n&lt;k exit;
2. partition A into k equal size parts
   A1 , A2 , … , Ak, (This takes √n steps)
3. for (i=1 to k)
     call R(Ak,k); // may change Ak;
4. merge A1 , A2 , … , Ak into new A with size n;
   (This takes k steps)
5. call Q(A);
6. return()</pre>There are 3 derived algorithms X,Y,Z, based on R. X sets k as 2, and its Q’s complexity is θ(m), m is the size of Q’s input. Y sets k as 4, and its Q’s complexity is θ(√m), m is input size. Z sets k as 9, and its Q’s complexity is θ(m), m is input size.<br>What following comparisons are true?

（複選）To analyze the complexity of the following procedure P, We will use the following assumptions: Suppose P and B are both procedures. B take θ(√m) time to compute, where m is the size of B’s input; each statement line in and outside the loop counts 1 step.<pre>Procedure P( array1[a1, a2, ..., an])
1. if n&lt;9 exit.
2. call B(array1[a1, a2, ..., an])
   declare new empty array2, array3, array4;
3. for (i=1 to n)
4. { if ((i mod 9)=0)  insert ai into array2;
5.   if ((i mod 9)=3)  insert ai into array3;
6.   if ((i mod 9)=6)  insert ai into array4 }
8. call P( array2 );
9. call P( array3 );
10. call P (array4);</pre>Which of the following relations on F<sub>n</sub> can describe the complexity of procedure P with respect to problem size n?

（複選）In the following procedure P, P and B are both procedures; each statement line in and outside the loop counts 1 step.<pre>Procedure P( array1[a1, a2, ..., an])
1. if n&lt;9 exit.
2. call B(array1[a1, a2, ..., an])
   declare new empty array2, array3, array4;
3. for (i=1 to n)
4. { if ((i mod 9)=1)  insert ai into array2;
5.   if ((i mod 9)=4)  insert ai into array3;
6.   if ((i mod 9)=7)  insert ai into array4 }
8. call P( array2 );
9. call P( array3 );
10. call P (array4);</pre>In order to make P’s complexity O(n) , which of the following can be B’s complexity? (m is the input size of B)
